{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_mismatch_3.march","start_line":9,"start_col":15,"end_line":9,"end_col":33,"message":"`tidy` takes a `Cap(IO.FileSystem)` parameter, but capability values were retired: a function no longer receives its authority, it uses the current authority, which `main`'s `needs` clause asks for and each operation checks.\nhelp: remove the parameter and the argument at each call; to state what `tidy` may use, give it a `needs` clause.","code":"cap_param_retired","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":9,"start_col":10,"end_line":9,"end_col":35,"text":""},{"kind":"replace","start_line":14,"start_col":17,"end_line":14,"end_col":21,"text":""}],"applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/cap_mismatch_3.march","start_line":13,"start_col":15,"end_line":13,"end_col":31,"message":"`main` asks for its authority with `Cap` parameters, which are deprecated and will be removed in the next release: a capability value grants nothing since the current authority replaced it.\nhelp: request it with a `needs` clause: `fn main() needs IO.FileRead do`.","code":"deprecated_main_cap","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":13,"start_col":9,"end_line":13,"end_col":32,"text":"()"},{"kind":"replace","start_line":13,"start_col":33,"end_line":13,"end_col":33,"text":"needs IO.FileRead "}],"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_mismatch_3.march","start_line":14,"start_col":17,"end_line":14,"end_col":19,"message":"`tidy` needs file-system access, but `fr` is the file-read capability.","code":"cap_mismatch:IO.FileSystem","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":14,"start_col":17,"end_line":14,"end_col":19,"text":"_cap_filesystem"},{"kind":"replace","start_line":13,"start_col":31,"end_line":13,"end_col":31,"text":", _cap_filesystem : Cap(IO.FileSystem)"}],"applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[{"file":"errors/cap_mismatch_3.march","start_line":14,"start_col":12,"end_line":14,"end_col":30,"message":"`tidy` needs `Cap(IO.FileSystem)`"},{"file":"errors/cap_mismatch_3.march","start_line":13,"start_col":10,"end_line":13,"end_col":12,"message":"`fr` was bound here as `Cap(IO.FileRead)`"},{"file":"errors/cap_mismatch_3.march","start_line":13,"start_col":9,"end_line":13,"end_col":32,"message":"`main` is granted only `Cap(IO.FileRead)` here"}],"notes":["`IO.FileRead` is a part of `IO.FileSystem`; it does not carry the rest of `IO.FileSystem`.","help: give `main` a `Cap(IO.FileSystem)` parameter and pass it to `tidy`."],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
